# Historical native V4 journal replay

Status: **PASS for historical-observation compatibility**. No native process was
executed during this review. This is current Python-reader replay of retained
published original bytes, not a current-source native cost measurement.

## Original source and archive

The package is retained in evidence publication commit
`c2297ad53fef1d9b552e657cfd205d583c91980d` at:

`evidence/pon-joint-resource-contract-20261109/archives/117-local-validation.tar.xz`

That evidence directory is not present in the current checkout HEAD
`da1374a200022bc14dc2bd325cc9ba29dbcd24ab`. It was recovered read-only from the
existing historical Git objects; checkout source files were not modified.

The exact original archive is retained here under `published-originals/archives/`:
976,596 bytes, SHA-256
`eeaa11ad8a6f565f989edf035d6cb5f59d45ed2956276c824b4daac7064ea8f6`,
Git blob `059549dfa206b04382322fb476db231ae49f1f55`.
All 105 file members, totaling 43,916,967 uncompressed bytes, matched the
published per-member size/SHA-256 inventory. The source documents and archive
also matched the original SHA256SUMS index. See `archive-validation.json`.

Source-before and source-after are byte-identical and bind historical native
source commit `11791e2da79b69322271be2cffe03725165151d1` and tree
`162552848110fda532504b78865a16930bc6d9bb`. The Git commit/tree relation and
26,124 tree entries were independently checked. The full historical checkout
was not recreated; its 2,485,379,627-byte worktree verification remains the
retained original recorder observation. The native V4 example, shared producer,
material constructor, and V2 fixed-material reader remain byte-identical between
that historical source and the current checkout. The current V4 reader is the
stricter revised file. See `source-and-process-validation.json`.

The retained gzip binary decompresses to 903,328 bytes with SHA-256
`bd74dea5a8b1ddc57e86f1d181c3cdb287321dc0b9651e03b6f21adfcfe2f45a`,
matching the before, loaded-executable, and after identities in both original
process receipts. Original journal/stderr hashes and native exits also match
those receipts. This checks retained bindings; it is not independent execution
authentication of the original machine.

