## Current reader identity and scope

The reader and its fixed-material helper hashes were checked before and after
both replays and did not change:

- V4 reader: `1d0fb8a0b0d0d3ba9be398801488e90feea7364c6adf5d805e06aa2c1811381b`.
- V2 helper: `6a967274b93394494a2606c08173d4c755f255742bdca6cecd9665ce9f3686fa`.

`replay-summary.json` is the concise machine-readable result. The result closes
the concrete compatibility risk that the stricter frozen recipes, support matrix,
and losing-proof digest checks reject this existing complete native campaign.
It does not replay the challenge-dependent W1 relation, produce a new native run,
authenticate actual resource use, prove a cheapest-legal-work lower bound, or
qualify public service. All qualification flags remain false and added consensus
credit remains zero.

The extracted originals are convenience copies. The complete original compressed
archive plus its inventory retain the exact raw bytes without requiring a second
publication of the 40 MB uncompressed journal.
